    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean \"proponents argue\" is just a way of saying it's a theory. if you look at the actual math of the transition costs vs the actual proven capacity of green tech to power a whole economy, the math just doesn't seem to add up for a stable transition. doesn't the reliance on massive government intervention and subsidies make the whole thing way more risky than just letting the market handle energy shifts naturally?",
